// MIDI → SoundFont — live polyphonic SF2 playback from a USB controller.
//
// Plug in a USB keyboard and play. `midi()` captures note-on/off events and
// dispatches them directly through `soundfont()`'s built-in 32-voice
// allocator — no `poly()` wrapper required. Preset 0 is Acoustic Grand
// Piano in the GM standard; edit the number to swap instruments (see
// `/docs/reference/builtins/soundfonts` for the GM preset table).
//
// Gain staging: each SoundFont voice is roughly unity per zone, so a 4-note
// chord sums to ~4× amplitude and clips `out()`. The `* gain` after
// `soundfont()` reserves headroom for held chords.

bpm = 120
gain = param("gain", 0.4, 0, 1)

midi()
    |> soundfont(@, "gm", 0) * gain
    |> out(@)
